course: dictionary
lesson: 12436
title: Measuring how loud a sound is
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A decibel is a unit for measuring how loud a sound is. A unit is a standard amount we use to measure something, like metres for length. Decibels are written as dB, so 60 dB means a sound measured at 60 decibels.
explain: The number tells you how loud a sound is. A bigger number means a louder sound. «A whisper is about 30 dB.» «Normal talk is about 60 dB.» Because 60 is bigger than 30, normal talk is louder than a whisper.
explain: Look at the clues in a sentence. «The rock concert was over 100 dB, so it was very loud.» The words over 100 tell you it is louder than the other sounds in this lesson. «Long exposure above about 85 dB can damage your hearing.» Exposure means being near a sound for a long time.
fact: A decibel is a unit for measuring how loud a sound is.
fact: The short form is dB, so 80 dB means 80 decibels.
fact: A whisper is about 30 dB, normal talk about 60 dB, and a busy road about 80 dB.
fact: A rock concert is often over 100 dB.
fact: Long exposure to sounds above about 85 dB can damage your hearing, so wear ear protection and keep headphones at a safe volume.
exercise: What is a decibel? | A type of musical instrument | A sound that is very high-pitched | A kind of ear protection | *A unit for measuring how loud a sound is
exercise: Which sound is the loudest in this lesson? | A busy road, about 80 dB | *A rock concert, over 100 dB | Whispering, about 30 dB | Normal talk, about 60 dB
exercise: Maya says «The busy road is about 80 dB.» Is that louder than normal talk at 60 dB? | Yes, because dB is a type of road | They are both the same | No, it is quieter | *Yes, because 80 is bigger than 60
test: What does the short form dB stand for? | Digital beat | Double bass | *Decibel | Distance band
test: Which sound could damage your hearing if you are near it for a long time? | *A sound above about 85 dB | A soft lullaby | A quiet bedroom
exam: Which is louder, a whisper of about 30 dB or a busy road of about 80 dB, and why? | They are equally loud | *The busy road, because 80 is more than 30 | You cannot tell from numbers | The whisper, because 30 is more than 80
